# IR receiver module (VS1838B), 38 kHz.
#
# A photodiode, an amplifier and a demodulator in one shielded package: aimed
# at a remote, OUT pulses low with the bursts it sees. Electrically it is its
# internal pull-up, about 33 kOhm from VCC to OUT, so OUT idles high; a press
# on the IR Remote part plays that button's NEC code out of OUT, timed to the
# cycle, into whichever Arduino pin it reaches — powered from 5 V or 3.3 V and
# grounded, as a real one must be. IRremote decodes it.
#
# Drawn by the `ir_receiver` painter: vector paths generated from the
# "IR Receiver" frame in the PinBench Parts Figma file by the Flutter Da Vinci
# plugin.

PART "IR Receiver (VS1838B)"
ALIAS "VS1838B"
ALIAS "Infrared Receiver"
ID ir_receiver
CATEGORY sensors
DESCRIPTION "38 kHz IR remote receiver — OUT, GND, VCC"

# Legs one hole pitch apart, OUT, GND, VCC from the left with the lens facing.
SIZE 40px 72px
PAINTER ir_receiver

PINS
  out  4px   68px  output  "OUT"
  gnd  20px  68px  ground  "GND"
  vcc  36px  68px  power   "VCC"

PHYSICS resistor
  # The internal pull-up from VCC to OUT.
  n1 = vcc
  n2 = out
  resistance = 33000
